    "narrative": "For the May 10th slate, the Zurich Zebras lean heavily into the top-of-the-order firepower against Sugano. **Trea Turner** (78.26) and **Kyle Schwarber** (74.75) represent our elite plays, capitalizing on a favorable 4.73 xERA matchup and prime batting order placement. **Yordan Alvarez** (72.28) remains a must-start despite facing a left-handed arm, as his elite xwOBA floor keeps his ceiling significantly higher than the rest of the cohort. Additionally, **Junior Caminero** (66.67) earns a UTIL start due to park factors and a favorable wind forecast, while **Caleb Durbin** (62.99) is a sneaky value play; his score is buoyed by favorable wind conditions and a matchup against a mediocre arm in Martinez, highlighting his utility even from the #9 spot.\n\nThe decision-making process for the remaining slots focused on aggressive platoon deployment. **Dillon Dingler** (60.86) is our most efficient catcher play today, riding a dynamic platoon advantage against Cameron. Conversely, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (52.12) and **Luke Raley** (52.04) are active but carry reduced efficiency scores due to opposing pitchers who excel at neutralizing stolen base attempts, a critical bottleneck for our 5x5 Roto strategy. **Carson Benge** was the toughest cut from the active lineup (47.25); while he provides a solid floor, his projected efficiency fell just short of the established threshold compared to the high-upside platoons of **Dillon Dingler** and **Caleb Durbin**. \n\nWe are monitoring lineup finalization for **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith** closely, as any shift from their projected spots could necessitate a recalibration. Risk management is paramount today, particularly with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** drawing a difficult assignment against deGrom, whose sub-3.20 xERA serves as a significant hurdle. While we wait for **Christian Yelich** to return from the IL and **Zac Veen** to be recalled from Albuquerque, the priority remains maximizing daily efficiency to maintain our edge in the steals category without burning through our limited game cap allotment.",
